   "text": {
    "L1": "A prime number has exactly two factors: 1 and itself.",
    "L2": "A composite number has more than two factors and can make a rectangle with more than one row.",
    "L3": "One is neither prime nor composite because it has only one factor. And 2 is the only even prime.",
    "L4": "Odd does not mean prime. For example, 21 is odd but 21 equals 3 times 7.",
    "L5": "Use a sieve: cross out multiples of 2, then 3, 5 and 7.",
    "L6": "The numbers left, except 1, are the primes up to 100.",
    "L7": "Try 51. Its digit sum is 6, so 3 is a factor and 51 equals 3 times 17.",
    "L8": "Now check the 40s. Tap the numbers that survive the sieve."
   },
